 blue-collar jobs.\n\n2.**Question Analysis:**.\n   - The question asks which option is intended to be pointed out in this paragraph.\n\n3.**Evaluate Each Option:**.\n   - **Option A:** "The major catalogue of secondary vocational education in China needs to be adjusted according to the actual post demand.".\n     - This option suggests that the catalogue should be updated to better align with the current job market.This aligns with the context\'s concern about the mismatch between the catalogue and the actual blue-collar jobs.\n   - **Option B:** "The professional education of secondary vocational education in China is unable to train students to enter blue-collar posts.".\nThe conclusion is that there is no problem with the current alignment between the catalogue and the actual jobs, and students are easily finding employment in blue-collar positions.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
