messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA committee works for two years and is composed of 4 members each year, 2 of which are from the following 4 judges: F, G, H and I, and the other 2 members are from the following 3 scientists: V, Y and Z. Each year, the committee is chaired by one member. A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year. The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year. The committee members must meet the following conditions: G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y cannot be members of this committee in the same year. Each year, only one of I and V is a member of this committee.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if H is the chairman in the first year, which of the followings can be the chairman in the second year?\n# Options:\nA) F\nB) G\nC) Y\nD) I', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, we need to consider the constraints given and determine the possible combinations for each year.Let's break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Committee Composition**: The committee consists of 4 members each year, with 2 judges (F, G, H, I) and 2 scientists (V, Y, Z).\n2.**Chairmanship**: The chairman must be a member of the committee and must retire during the second year.\n3.Stagnation: A member who chairs the first year must continue during the second year.\n4.**Possibilities**: G and V can be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y can be members of the committee in the same year. Both I and V can be members of the committee each year.\n\nGiven that H is the chairman in the first year, we need to determine the possible members for the second year\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
