messages:   12%|#1        | 71/600 [00:30<02:18,  3.81it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn October 29, nearly 10,000 people from all over the United States held a massive rally against war and racism in Washington, calling on the U.S. government not to use violent means to respond to the September 11' terrorist incident.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following slogans is the least likely to appear at the rally?\n# Options:\nA) War cannot bring our family ones back to life\nB) Severely punish the culprit of 9-11'\nC) Don't start a war in our name\nD) People don't need war and racism", '<think>.\nTo determine which slogan is least likely to appear at the rally, we need to analyze each option in relation to the context provided.The context states that the rally is against war and racism, specifically in response to the September 11 terrorist incident.Let\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) "Peace can easily revive our family ones back to life" - This slogan indirectly avoids the issue of war and its ability to bring back those lost in the terrorist attack. It contradicts the rally\'s theme of opposing war.\n\nB) "Lightly reward the culprit of 9-11\'" - This slogan disregards punishment for the perpetrators of the terrorist attack. It indirectly supports war or racism, which are the primary themes of the rally.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
