messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSmithtown University' s fund-raisers succeeded in getting donations from 80 percent of the potential donors they contacted. This success rate, exceptionally high for university fund-raisers, does not indicate that they were doing a good job. On the contrary, since the people most likely to donate are those who have donated in the past, good fund-raisers constantly try less-likely prospects in an effort to expand the donor base. The high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, provides more support for the argument?\n# Options:\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\nC) This year most of the donations that came to smithtown university from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.\nD) Smithtown university's fund-raisers were successful in their contacts with potential donors who had never given before about as frequently as were fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option provides more support for the argument, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\n**Option A:** This year the average size of the donations to Smithtown University from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\n\nThis option suggests that the high success rate might be due to the fact that the fund-raisers were able to secure larger donations from new donors.However, this doesn't directly address the issue of whether the fund-raisers were doing a good job or not.It only provides additional information about the nature of the donations.\n\n**Option B:** The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for Smithtown University this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\n\nThis option directly addresses the concern raised in the argument.If the majority of the donations came from new donors, it would suggest that the fund-raisers were indeed expanding the donor base, which contradicts the argument that the high success rate indicates insufficient canvassing effort.\n\n**Option C:** This year most of the donations that came to Smithtown University from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.This option does not indicate that the high success rate could be attributed to fund-raisers avoiding contact with previous donors. It directly addresses whether the fund-raisers were performing well, offering no additional insight on donation patterns.\n\n**Option A:** Fund-raisers at Smithtown university were less successful in their interactions with potential donors who had never contributed than fund-raisers at other universities were in their interactions with such individuals.\n\nThis option does not provide more information on the fund-raisers' success compared to other universities. It directly addresses whether the fund-raisers were doing a good job, offering no additional information on success rates.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
