laiming land from the lake and building dikes to kill snails have separated the waters of Dongting Lake.\n- This option indicates that human activities have altered the natural habitat of the lake, potentially affecting the ecosystem.This supports the expert's point of view that the ecological environment has been destroyed, leading to a rat disaster.\n\nThe rise in water level of Dongting Lake during the flood season every year typically does not lead to the drowning of many rats, as the severe drought last year prevented much of an increase in water level.\n- This information suggests that the flooding of the lake during the flood season does not serve as a control mechanism for the rat population. The lack of significant rise in water level due to the severe drought supports the belief that the ecological balance has not been disrupted.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
