messages:   45%|####5     | 270/600 [02:39<01:57,  2.80it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA class plans to select two from three girls, including Fang Rufen, Guo Yanran, and He Zhilian, and three from five boys, including Peng Youwen, Qiu Zhijie, Ren Xiangyang, Song Wenkai, and Tang Xiaohua, to form a group of five college students to teach on a voluntary basis in the mountain area. Requirements: (1) Guo Yanran and Tang Xiaohua are not selected at the same time; (2) Peng Youwen and Song Wenkai are not selected at the same time; (3) Qiu Zhijie and Tang Xiaohua are not selected at the same time.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if Tang Xiaohua is selected, which of the following two must be selected?\n# Options:\nA) Fang rufen and guo yanran\nB) Guo yanran and he zhilian\nC) Peng youwen and he zhilian\nD) Fang rufen and he zhilian', "<think>.\nTo solve this problem, we need to analyze the given constraints and determine which options are valid when Tang Xiaohua is selected.Let's break down the constraints:.\n\n1.Guo Yanran and Tang Xiaohua cannot be selected at the same time.\n2.Peng Youwen and Song Wenkai cannot be selected at the same time.\n3.Qiu Zhijie and Tang Xiaohua cannot be selected at the same time.\n\nSince Tang Xiaohua is selected, we can eliminate any options that include her.This leaves us with:.\n\nA) Fang Rufen and Guo Yanran.\nB) Guo Yanran and He Zhilian.\nC) Peng Youwen and He Zhilian.\nD) Fang Rufen and He Zhilian.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) Fang Rufen and Guo Yanran: This option is valid because Guo Yanran is not selected, and there are no other conflicting constraints.\nB) Guo Yanran and He Zhilian: This option is valid because Guo Yanran is not selected, and there are no other conflicting constraints.Neither Fang Rufen nor Guo Yanran should be selected, and there are several conflicting constraints present. Tang Xiaohua should not be chosen, and both options are invalid.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
