messages:   48%|####7     | 285/600 [02:45<02:34,  2.04it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option does not fit the definition of the broken window effect.The broken window effect refers to the idea that if something is broken or damaged, it will lead to more damage or destruction.Let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n- This option describes a situation where one act (not cleaning graffiti) leads to another act (more graffiti).This fits the broken window effect definition.\n\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n- This option describes a situation where one act (treating pollution) leads to another act (preserving the cleanliness of the entire basin).This fits the broken window effect definition.\n\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will refrain from throwing their rubbish away and will feel ashamed.\n- This option describes a situation where one act (rubbish in a clean place) leads to another act (avoiding throwing more rubbish).This fits the broken window effect definition\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
