 reduce the number of village deaths attributable to viruses, and the plan involves cutting off passageways that allow the bat to emerge from its caves.If the plan is successful, the bat should no longer be able to emerge and spread the viruses.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) If the spotted fruit bat is the only one that serves as a reservoir for deadly viruses, and eliminating it would prevent the spread of these viruses, then this option supports the government's plan.However, it does not directly indicate that the plan will not lead to its objective.\nIf government workers have successfully penetrated completely into the caves where the spotted fruit bat dwells, this indicates that the bat may not be able to emerge and spread viruses. This option suggests that the plan may be effective in achieving its objective.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
