e as much as a party would expect from 30% of eligible voters.This would strengthen the argument by showing that the current level of support is sufficient to make the party viable.\n\nB) This option proposes that an education party could be viable with a smaller base than is typically required.This would weaken the argument because it suggests that the current level of support is not enough to make the party viable.\n\nBased on the analysis, options B, C, and D all strengthen the argument by suggesting that the current level of support is sufficient to make the party viable.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
