messages:   56%|#####6    | 336/600 [03:12<01:51,  2.36it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, community banks in some big cities have been closed frequently. At the same time, a series of new banks, such as unmanned banks, 5G banks and smart banks, keep emerging. Bank branches are bidding farewell to cold glass counters and metal benches. The traditional transaction processing functions of bank branches are weakened, and customized services, product experience, social interaction and other functions are increasingly prominent. As a result, some experts predict that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, best supports the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening", "<think>.\nTo determine which option best supports the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years, we need to analyze each option and see how it relates to the trend of technological advancements and the changing nature of banking services.\n\nOption A suggests that customers need to spend a lot of time waiting in line at the bank branch.This could be seen as a negative aspect of traditional banking, but it doesn't directly address the technological changes that are making bank branches less necessary.\n\nOption B mentions the introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means, which is a clear indication of how technology is transforming the banking industry.This supports the idea that traditional bank branches may become less relevant as technology takes over some of their functions.\n\nOption C suggests that traditional bank branches will eventually become obsolete due to advancements in online banking and mobile banking. This implies that face-to-face interaction will no longer be necessary and complex transactions can be conducted solely through digital platforms.\n\nOption D argues that the importance of bank branches is diminishing as online and mobile banking gain traction. However, this doesn't offer a clear answer to the question of whether traditional bank branches will still be around in the next two decades.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
