ekly support group meetings gives patients less faith in the standard treatment for disease T, this could imply that the meetings might actually be harmful or ineffective.However, this does not directly address whether the meetings help patients live longer or not.Attending weekly support group meetings is an essential part of the standard medical treatment for various diseases, indicating that the meetings are specific to disease T and not part of a broader treatment plan. This directly undermines the argument about disease T.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
