messages:   75%|#######4  | 449/600 [04:17<01:27,  1.74it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAvoidance conditioning refers to when a situation of disgust or unhappiness arises, the individual reacts in a way that escapes the situation of disgust or unhappiness. Then the probability of this reaction occurring in similar scenarios later increases.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is not avoidance conditioning?\n# Options:\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand\nC) Leave temporarily when you feel noisy in the house\nD) Afraid to meet strangers and dare not go to the streets', "<think>.\nTo determine which option is not avoidance conditioning, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road: This is an example of avoidance conditioning.Seeing garbage on the road can cause disgust or unhappiness, leading to a detour to avoid the situation.The individual reacts in a way that escapes the situation, increasing the probability of this reaction occurring in similar scenarios later.\n\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand: This is also an example of avoidance conditioning.Hitting something hot can cause pain or discomfort, leading to a quick withdrawal of the hand to avoid the situation.The individual reacts in a way that escapes the situation, increasing the probability of this reaction occurring in similar scenarios later.Not being afraid to meet strangers and feeling comfortable going to the streets is an example of avoidance conditioning. Embracing new encounters and public spaces can lead to positive experiences, reinforcing the individual's willingness to engage in similar situations in the future.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
