messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given statement and analyze each option step by step.\n\nThe original statement is: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis can be translated into a logical implication: If P (you close all the wrong doors), then Q (truth will be shut out).In logical terms, this is represented as P → Q.\n\nNow, let\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nThis can be represented as Q → P. This is the contrapositive of the original statement, which is logically equivalent to the original statement.Therefore, this option is correct.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nThis can be represented as ~Q → ~P.This is the converse of the original statement, which is not logically equivalent to the original statement.Therefore, this option is incorrect.To reject the truth, we must accept wrong.\nThis statement directly contradicts the original statement by emphasizing the acceptance of wrong and rejection of truth.Therefore, this option is correct.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
