messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nZhao Ming, Qian Hong and Sun Jie were admitted to Peking University, Tsinghua University and Beijing normal University. About which school they were admitted to, the students made the following guesses: classmate A guessed: Zhao Ming was admitted by Tsinghua University and Sun Jie was admitted by Beijing normal University. Classmate B guess: Zhao Ming was admitted by Beijing normal University and Qian Hong was admitted by Tsinghua University. Classmate C guess: Zhao Ming was admitted to Peking University and Sun Jie was admitted to Tsinghua University. As a result, the students' guesses were half right.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is their correct admission?\n# Options:\nA) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, tsinghua university and beijing normal university respectively.\nB) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to tsinghua university, beijing normal university and peking university respectively.\nC) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to beijing normal university, tsinghua university and peking university respectively.\nD) Zhao ming, qian hong and sun jie were admitted to peking university, beijing normal university and tsinghua university respectively.", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to analyze the given information and determine which option is consistent with the students' guesses being half right.Let's break down the problem step by step:.\n\n1.**Understand the Students' Guesses:**.\n   - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Peking University), Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University).\n   - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University).\n   - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University).\n\n2.**Analyze the Half-Right Condition:**.\n   - If a student's guess is half right, it means that exactly one part of their guess is true and the other part is false.\n\n3.**Evaluate Each Option:**.\n   - **Option A:** Zhao Ming (Peking University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University), Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University).\n     - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University) is true.\n     - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Qian Hong (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University) is true.\n     - All guesses are true, so this option is not half right.\n\n   - **Option B:** Zhao Ming (Tsinghua University), Qian Hong (Beijing Normal University), Sun Jie (Peking University).\n     - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua University) is true, Sun Jie (Beijing Normal University) is true.\n     - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua University) is true, Qian Hong (Beijing Normal University) is true.\n     - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Tsinghua University) is true, Sun Jie (Peking University) is true.\n     - All guesses are true, so this option is not half right.\n\n   - **Option C:** Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University), Qian Hong (Peking University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University).\n     - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University) is true, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University) is true, Qian Hong (Peking University) is true.\n     - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Beijing Normal University) is true, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - All guesses are true, so this option is not half right.\n\n   - **Option D:** Zhao Ming (Peking University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University).\n     - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Qian Hong (Tsinghua University) is true.Incorrect Option:**.\n   - **Option D:** Zhao Ming (Peking University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University).\n     - Classmate A: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - Classmate B: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Qian Hong (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - Classmate C: Zhao Ming (Peking University) is true, Sun Jie (Tsinghua University) is true.\n     - All guesses are true, so this option is not half right.\n\nAfter re-evaluating, we realize that all of the options satisfy the half-right condition.However, if we consider the accuracy of the problem statement or the interpretation, we can conclude that the incorrect answer is:.\n\n**Option D:** Zhao Ming (Peking University), Qian Hong (Tsinghua University), Sun Jie (Tsinghua University)\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]] 82%|########2 | 494/600 [04:45<01:00,  1.75it/s]
