states that not all candidates will be hired.Therefore, this option cannot lead to the conclusion that all candidates will not be hired.\n\n**Option C:** "In this recruitment examination, there are bound to be candidates who will not be hired."\n- This statement is false based on the given information. The given information explicitly states that due to the limited recruitment positions, it is possible for all candidates to be hired. This means that there might not be candidates who will not be hired. Therefore, this option leads to the conclusion that all candidates will be hired.\n\n**Option D:** "In this recruitment examination, there might not be candidates to be hired."\n- This statement is necessarily true based on the given information. The statement implies that there might not be candidates who will be hired, but the given information only states that not all candidates will be hired. Therefore, this option can lead to the conclusion that all candidates will be hired.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is **Option A**.\n\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
