stood as sophistication and flattery.It emphasizes that the core of emotional intelligence is not just about recognizing and controlling one's own emotions but also about communicating with others and integrating into the collective.The success of this development depends heavily on parental involvement in daily life.\nGiven this context, the most illogical next step would be to ignore how parents can ineffectively practice emotional intelligence in their daily lives. This would involve misunderstanding the irrelevance of emotional intelligence, overlooking its role in child development, and passively avoiding activities that promote emotional intelligence within the family.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
