mpany.If this is true, then the success of a new company is not solely dependent on the financing channel, but rather on the quality of management.This would weaken the claim that financing channels are more important than other factors.\n\nWhen deciding whether to fund a startup, VCs do not need to consider factors such as the entrepreneur's personal qualities or the company's strategic plan.This statement implies that venture capitalists only focus on one factor when deciding to provide funding. This means that the success of a new company is solely dependent on the financing channel, which would strengthen the claim that financing channels are more important than other factors.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
