 flow to the northwest.\n- This option implies that if fame and wealth do not exist for a long time, the Han River should not flow to the northwest.The context clearly indicates that fame and wealth are everlasting and will always be present.\n\nC) Fame and wealth cannot always be there.\n- This option suggests that fame and wealth can always be present, which contradicts the context's assertion that their existence is not guaranteed forever.\n\nD) If the Han river can flow to the northwest, then fame and wealth will always be there.\n- This option implies that the presence of fame and wealth is dependent on the Han River flowing to the northwest. However, the context does not mention any connection between the river's direction and the existence of fame and wealth.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
