ferent from the surrounding areas. This is not an environmental effect because it is not caused by human activities (fossil fuel use) and does not lead to changes in the structure and function of the environmental system (temperature remains stable).\n\nOption D: A coastal city preserved the sea to maintain its natural state, and a small town with a capacity of 70,000 people was not built on the island. This is an environmental effect because it involves preserving the natural environment and avoiding human activities that could disrupt the environmental system. It is a conscious decision to protect the landform and ecosystem, which is directly related to preventing environmental changes caused by natural processes or human activities.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
